{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UjrYiJD698DHAZENf5YDH8","type":"tool_result","content":"53:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/overview_schematic.png}\n78:Table~\\ref{tab:cases} lists the eight cases; full parameters are in Supplementary Table~\\ref{tab:spec}. The outcome mean is $\\mu_i(\\mathbf z)=1+x_i^\\top\\beta+(\\tau_0+\\tau_1x_{i1})z_i+h_i(\\mathbf z)$ with $\\beta=(0.8,-0.5)$, $\\tau_0=1$, $\\tau_1=0.5$ and an interference term $h_i$ built from the neighbour-treated fraction $f_i=\\sum_jA_{ij}z_j/\\max(d_i,1)$:\n117:Model selection used eight seeds (101--108) on the same eight case specifications; three estimator classes were each scored once there (Supplementary Table~\\ref{tab:search}). One estimator was then frozen and evaluated once on 24 seeds (9001--9024) with fresh graphs and assignments, which is the evidence for all headline numbers. No invalid or failed runs occurred on the final plane. The final evaluation completed with outcome \\emph{qualified}; this means the evaluator's declared requirements were met on this grid and does not by itself establish validity, generality or superiority beyond it. Because case specifications are shared between model selection and final scoring, the final gain over the linear baseline measures behaviour on new seeds of known mechanism families, not transfer to new mechanisms.\n123:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/main_accuracy.pdf}\n201:\\includegraphics[width=0.72\\textwidth]{figures/reliability.pdf}\n243:\\section{Supplementary Information}\n319:\\subsection{LLM Usage}\n.claude/skills/validate-paper/:\nSKILL.md\nscripts\ntemplates\n\n.claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts:\ncompile_latex.sh\nvalidate_compile_inputs.py\nvalidate_figures.py\nvalidate_rendered_si.py\nvalidate_tex_refs.py","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60d3a1a1-ddb2-4ab9-a270-799bebf6b6bb","uuid":"31a8a361-0881-4570-b06d-910dd7844187","timestamp":"2026-11-11T0