{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TrmZL7CRpFGMgKqTgiv9Jy","type":"tool_result","content":"qualified completed True\n['final.qualification.correct', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.status']\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py\", line 9, in <module>\n    from src.orchestrator.paper_step import read_json, validate_figure_manifest\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'src'\nValidated sections and 28 citation key references.\n117:Model selection used eight seeds (101--108) on the same eight case specifications; three estimator classes were each scored once there (Supplementary Table~\\ref{tab:search}). One estimator was then frozen and evaluated once on 24 seeds (9001--9024) with fresh graphs and assignments, which is the evidence for all headline numbers. No invalid or failed runs occurred on the final plane. The final evaluation completed with outcome \\emph{qualified}; this means the evaluator's declared requirements were met on this grid and does not by itself establish validity, generality or superiority beyond it. Because case specifications are shared between model selection and final scoring, the final gain over the linear baseline measures behaviour on new seeds of known mechanism families, not transfer to new mechanisms.\n156:Two aspects need qualification. First, the gap to the linear baseline is 0.054 on a plane mean, % @evidence[[derived_stats.json#frozen_vs_linear_abs_gap]]\n230:\\paragraph{Limitations.} (1) Case specifications are shared between model selection and final scoring, and the library was designed after seeing model-selection per-case errors; the final result is out-of-sample over seeds but not over mechanisms. (2) There is a single graph size ($n=3000$) and a single assignment probability (0.5). (3) Contrasts are single case pairs, not a factorial design; they are not accompanied by per-case intervals, and several pairs vary more than one property. (4) Per-case values for the baselines, the bias, and the coverage are unavailable, so we make no per-case baseline comparison. (5) The cause of the larger errors in cases 6--8 (including the two-hop failure) and of the undercoverage is not established, and the mapping selected per case was not verified, so the mapping-mismatch account is a hypothesis. (6) There was no ablation of the gate margin or library components, so we cannot attribute the gain over linear regression to any particular mapping or to the gate itself; only three estimator classes were scored once on the model-selection seeds, and their per-case results are not used. (7) All mechanisms are synthetic; we ran no experiment on public graphs (e.g., Facebook100), real outcomes, learned graph representations, or other designs. (8) Qualification of the final evaluation is a statement about the measured result on this grid.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60d3a1a1-ddb2-4ab9-a270-799bebf6b6bb","uuid":"616f0df7-d653-445c-9199-ed3dd7f663b1","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:56:34.641Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"qualified completed True\n['final.qualification.correct', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.status']\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py\", line 9, in <module>\n    from src.orchestrator.paper_step import read_json, validate_figure_manifest\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'src'\nValidated sections and 28 citation key references.\n117:Model selection used eight seeds (101--108) on the same eight case specifications; three estimator classes were each scored once there (Supplementary Table~\\ref{tab:search}). One estimator was then frozen and evaluated once on 24 seeds (9001--9024) with fresh graphs and assignments, which is the evidence for all headline numbers. No invalid or failed runs occurred on the final plane. The final evaluation completed with outcome \\emph{qualified}; this means the evaluator's declared requirements were met on this grid and does not by itself establish validity, generality or superiority beyond it. Because case specifications are shared between model selection and final scoring, the final gain over the linear baseline measures behaviour on new seeds of known mechanism families, not transfer to new mechanisms.\n156:Two aspects need qualification. First, the gap to the linear baseline is 0.054 on a plane mean, % @evidence[[derived_stats.json#frozen_vs_linear_abs_gap]]\n230:\\paragraph{Limitations.} (1) Case specifications are shared between model selection and final scoring, and the library was designed after seeing model-selection per-case errors; the final result is out-of-sample over seeds but not over mechanisms. (2) There is a single graph size ($n=3000$) and a single assignment probability (0.5). (3) Contrasts are single case pairs, not a factorial design; they are not accompanied by per-case intervals, and several pairs vary more than one property. (4) Per-case values for the baselines, the bias, and the coverage are unavailable, so we make no per-case baseline comparison. (5) The cause of the larger errors in cases 6--8 (including the two-hop failure) and of the undercoverage is not established, and the mapping selected per case was not verified, so the mapping-mismatch account is a hypothesis. (6) There was no ablation of the gate margin or library components, so we cannot attribute the gain over linear regression to any particular mapping or to the gate itself; only three estimator classes were scored once on the model-selection seeds, and their per-case results are not used. (7) All mechanisms are synthetic; we ran no experiment on public graphs (e.g., Facebook100), real outcomes, learned graph representations, or other designs. (8) Qualification of the final evaluation is a statement about the measured result on this grid.","stderr":"","interrupte